[32m+[m[32m## Overview[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**LFC Reporting Hub** brings the major parts of a station's reporting workflow into one application.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstead of relying on disconnected manual processes, the platform provides structured data entry, flexible input methods, bank-statement processing, report generation, version history, delegate support, and offline-first capabilities in a single PWA.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> Built to make recurring reporting more structured, traceable, and efficient.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What It Does[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Capability | Description |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Multiple Input Methods** | Capture information through structured forms, WhatsApp text, voice input, or bank statements. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Report Generation** | Generate Excel reports using configured church reporting templates. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Bank Reconciliation** | Process uploaded bank statements with OCR and flag potential discrepancies. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Version History** | Preserve report changes with a complete version trail instead of hard-deleting data. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Delegate System** | Pair backup delegate accounts through temporary pairing codes. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Offline Support** | Continue working with an offline-first PWA architecture and queued data persistence. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Auto-Compile** | Support scheduled monthly report compilation through database-side scheduling. |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Core Features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Data Collection[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe platform supports several ways to get reporting information into the system:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Manual entry** — structured forms based on canonical reporting fields[m
[32m+[m[32m- **WhatsApp parsing** — interpret flexible WhatsApp text formats[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Voice input** — Web Speech API with preview and confirmation before saving[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Bank statement OCR** — extract information from uploaded statements using Tesseract.js[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Report Generation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReport generation is handled through Supabase Edge Functions and ExcelJS, allowing the application to produce Excel reports from configured templates and field mappings.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Bank Reconciliation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBank statements can be uploaded and processed through OCR. Extracted information can then be compared against report data, with discrepancy flags available for potential mismatches.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Versioned Reporting[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReports are treated as versioned records rather than disposable documents.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis provides:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Historical versions[m
[32m+[m[32m- Auditability[m
[32m+[m[32m- Safer updates[m
[32m+[m[32m- Server-side timestamps[m
[32m+[m[32m- Conflict-resolution support[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Offline-First Experience[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe PWA architecture uses IndexedDB persistence and TanStack Query to support queued work when connectivity is unavailable or unreliable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Delegate Support[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTemporary pairing codes allow stations to connect backup delegate accounts without replacing the primary station workflow.[m
[32m+[m
